.TH XRV-CLIENT 1 "November 2026" "XRV Client 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xrv-client \- encrypted relay client with an authenticated local SOCKS5 proxy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xrv-client
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xrv-client
is the Linux client for the XRV encrypted relay. It starts a SOCKS5 listener
on
.B 127.0.0.1
that requires a generated username and password, forwards TCP sessions through
the encrypted relay, probes Google edge addresses, and provides a live tunnel
test and logs.
.PP
It is the Linux counterpart of the Android app's proxy-only mode. Android TUN
and per-app routing are provided by Android's VpnService; on Linux, point
applications at the local proxy or use the system's VPN tooling.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Configure deployment IDs, the tunnel key, the local port, credentials, and a
Google edge. The command tests the four standard Google edges by default.
.TP
.B run
Start the authenticated local SOCKS5 proxy in the foreground.
.TP
.B probe
Test the configured Google edge candidates. Use
.B --write
to save the fastest edge.
.TP
.B test
Request
.B https://api.ipify.org
through the local proxy and print the exit IP, latency, and direct IP.
.TP
.B check
Check the process, listener, live tunnel, and direct IP.
.TP
.B status
Show whether the client is running and whether the listener is open.
.TP
.B stop
Stop the background client.
.TP
.B logs
Show the last 500 log lines.
.TP
.B config
Show the non-secret configuration with the tunnel key and proxy credentials
redacted.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/xrv/client.json
Encrypted-relay configuration, mode 600.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/xrv/client.log
Private log file with keys, deployment IDs, and proxy credentials redacted.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/xrv/client.pid
Process ID for the running client.
.SH SECURITY
The configuration contains the tunnel key. Never share it. The local proxy
requires a generated RFC 1929 username and password. The client never logs
payloads or secrets.
.SH SEE ALSO
.I /usr/share/doc/xrv-client/GUIDE.md
